---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Profile - Shri Omar Abdullah (Hon'ble Chief Minister)" 
  description="Official profile of Shri Omar Abdullah, the Hon'ble Chief Minister and Minister Incharge for Power Development Department of the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir."
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav class="text-xs text-gray-500" aria-label="Breadcrumbs">
      <ol class="flex gap-2">
        <li><a href="/" class="hover:underline focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-[#0B4F9C] rounded px-1">Home</a></li>
        <li>/</li>
        <li><span class="text-gray-400">Key Dignitaries</span></li>
        <li>/</li>
        <li><span class="font-semibold text-[#0B4F9C]">Shri Omar Abdullah</span></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- Back Button -->
    <div>
      <a 
        href="/" 
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 border border-slate-200 hover:border-[#0B4F9C] text-xs font-bold text-slate-600 hover:text-white hover:bg-[#0B4F9C] rounded transition-[background-color,border-color,color] duration-150 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-[#0B4F9C]/50"
      >
        <Icon name="arrow-left" size={12} strokeWidth={2.5} /> Back to Home
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Container -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      
      <!-- Left Column: Portrait Card & Stats -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-[#BDD7EE] p-6 shadow-sm text-center">
          <div class="w-36 h-36 rounded-full overflow-hidden bg-white mx-auto border-4 border-[#BDD7EE]/50 shadow-sm relative">
            <img 
              src="/dignitaries/omar_abdullah.png" 
              alt="Shri Omar Abdullah" 
              width="144" 
              height="144" 
              class="w-full h-full object-cover object-top"
            />
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-[#0B4F9C] mt-4 text-balance">Shri Omar Abdullah</h2>
          <div class="mt-2">
            <span class="inline-block text-[10px] text-[#0B4F9C] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-[#EAF4FF] px-2.5 py-1 rounded border border-[#BDD7EE]/50">
              Hon'ble Chief Minister
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest mt-2">UT of Jammu and Kashmir</p>
          <p class="text-[9px] text-[#D8681B] font-extrabold uppercase mt-1 leading-snug">Minister Incharge: PDD</p>
          
          <div class="w-12 h-0.5 bg-[#D8681B] mx-auto mt-4 rounded-full"></div>
          
          <div class="mt-4 text-left text-xs space-y-2.5 bg-[#EAF4FF]/40 p-4 rounded-xl border border-[#BDD7EE]/30 text-slate-700">
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <span class="text-slate-500 font-semibold">Assumed Office</span>
              <span class="font-bold text-slate-800">October 16, 2024</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <span class="text-slate-500 font-semibold">Education</span>
              <span class="font-bold text-slate-800 text-right">B.Com, Sydenham College</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <span class="text-slate-500 font-semibold">Office Location</span>
              <span class="font-bold text-slate-800 text-right">Civil Secretariat, J&K</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right Column: Biography & Career details -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-6">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-[#BDD7EE] p-6 md:p-8 shadow-sm space-y-6">
          
          <!-- Heading Section -->
          <div>
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-[#0B4F9C] text-balance">Official Profile</h1>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Detailed administrative background and biographical summary of the Chief Minister.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 1: Biography -->
          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-[#0B4F9C] uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-slate-100 pb-1.5">Biography</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-pretty">
              Shri Omar Abdullah assumed office as the Chief Minister of the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir on October 16, 2024. In addition to leading the administration as Chief Minister, he holds direct administrative oversight of key policy portfolios, including serving as the Minister Incharge for the Power Development Department (PDD).
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-pretty">
              He was born on March 10, 1970, in Rochford, Essex, United Kingdom. He completed his early education at the Lawrence School, Sanawar and subsequently earned his Bachelor of Commerce (B.Com) from Sydenham College in Mumbai. Coming from a prominent political family, Shri Abdullah has had a long and active career in both national and state governance.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- Section 2: Political & Administrative Career -->
          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-[#0B4F9C] uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-slate-100 pb-1.5">Public & Ministerial Career</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-pretty">
              Shri Omar Abdullah entered active politics in 1998, when he was elected to the 12th Lok Sabha from the Srinagar constituency at the age of 28, making him one of the youngest Members of Parliament. He was re-elected in 1999 and 2004, serving as a voice for the region in national policy circles.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-pretty">
              His service history includes key portfolios:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-slate-600 space-y-1 text-pretty">
              <li><strong>Union Minister of State for Commerce and Industry (1999–2001):</strong> Promoted international trade, industrial corridor planning, and regional trade partnerships.</li>
              <li><strong>Union Minister of State for External Affairs (2001–2002):</strong> Represented India's diplomatic missions abroad and oversaw regional passport and visa facilitation programs.</li>
              <li><strong>Chief Minister of Jammu &amp; Kashmir (2009–2015):</strong> Served as the youngest Chief Minister of the state, initiating extensive administrative, infrastructure, and tourism developments.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
